      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I see what you\u0027re trying to catch.\n\nBut I don\u0027t think you got it quite right. I think there\u0027s at least three bugs here (at least per the CommonMark spec), although I didn\u0027t actually test this to be sure:\n\nThe first is that \"```foo``` bar\" will not be treated as code span followed by regular text, it\u0027ll be treated as if it\u0027s starting a fenced code block.\n\nThe second is that you\u0027ll treat:\n\n```\n```bar\n```\n\nas if the \"```bar\" line ends the code block, when it shouldn\u0027t (i.e., you need to check for non-space trailing content when looking for the ending fence).\n\nThe third is that the fence is only allowed to have up to three leading spaces before the triple-backquote. You\u0027ll allow an arbitrary number of them.\n\nWhether it\u0027s worth handling all of these cases, I\u0027m not sure. I\u0027ll +1 this just because it\u0027s at least an improvement over nothing at all.",
      "parentUuid": "118d3420_37e99b5e",
      "revId": "5ce6e03a07129b090bdcc9399c4be5301d379131",
